00:00:00.380 --> 00:00:02.520
Let's get to unemployment.

00:00:02.520 --> 00:00:08.670
We have a situation right now where to stop
the virus from spreading to stop the invisible

00:00:08.670 --> 00:00:10.590
scourge or scored.

00:00:10.590 --> 00:00:13.139
Just Trump calls it from spreading noticed.

00:00:13.139 --> 00:00:16.739
By the way, Trump has not mentioned the Chinese
virus in his last three press conferences.

00:00:16.739 --> 00:00:17.749
Clearly somebody got to him.

00:00:17.749 --> 00:00:21.179
But now the invisible enemy, the invisible
scourge is what he says.

00:00:21.179 --> 00:00:22.970
We need people to stay home.

00:00:22.970 --> 00:00:24.199
That's the point.

00:00:24.199 --> 00:00:25.199
For some people.

00:00:25.199 --> 00:00:30.019
This merely means you work from home and not
much changes for others.

00:00:30.019 --> 00:00:34.700
For many people, this means their employer
is closing down.

00:00:34.700 --> 00:00:39.110
They no longer have a job, or at least they
don't have one until things open back up,

00:00:39.110 --> 00:00:43.820
which Donald Trump wants to apparently start
doing around Easter time.

00:00:43.820 --> 00:00:46.730
He wants the churches packed for Easter.

00:00:46.730 --> 00:00:53.140
We now have a report about the number of new
unemployment claims this past week, and the

00:00:53.140 --> 00:00:59.910
number is three million, three million, two
hundred and eighty three thousand.

00:00:59.910 --> 00:01:06.030
This is a staggering number when you look
at new claims per week going all the way back

00:01:06.030 --> 00:01:07.420
to the mid 1960s.

00:01:07.420 --> 00:01:09.950
It is a stunning number.

00:01:09.950 --> 00:01:15.679
Now, to give you some context, the expected
new claims for last week, we get the numbers

00:01:15.679 --> 00:01:16.679
the week after.

00:01:16.679 --> 00:01:18.069
So that's why we're looking at last week.

00:01:18.069 --> 00:01:20.090
This week could be even worse.

00:01:20.090 --> 00:01:23.270
Expected new claims last week were 1.6 million.

00:01:23.270 --> 00:01:24.340
That's what we were expecting.

00:01:24.340 --> 00:01:30.270
Economists actual claims came in at just under
3.3 million.

00:01:30.270 --> 00:01:34.490
Actual claims doubling the expected new claims.

00:01:34.490 --> 00:01:42.889
And for reference, the previous record for
new claims in a week was in 1982 when there

00:01:42.889 --> 00:01:46.219
were six hundred and ninety five thousand
new claims.

00:01:46.219 --> 00:01:51.329
Now, of course, you've got to adjust for population
growth in the United States, but still a crooked

00:01:51.329 --> 00:01:53.119
number to take a baseball phrase.

00:01:53.119 --> 00:01:55.710
Of course, all these numbers from the U.S.
Department of Labor.

00:01:55.710 --> 00:01:57.259
So this was last week.

00:01:57.259 --> 00:02:03.579
Now, since the reporting is on a delay, this
week's numbers will come in next week.

00:02:03.579 --> 00:02:10.670
This week's numbers could be even worse because
we've seen more states start to shut down

00:02:10.670 --> 00:02:13.330
and we could see potentially even worse numbers
next week.

00:02:13.330 --> 00:02:18.400
Now, if you're looking for anything, anything,
anything at all to mitigate the obvious absolute

00:02:18.400 --> 00:02:23.270
and total disaster of these numbers, there
is one thing that I will say, and this does

00:02:23.270 --> 00:02:25.160
not this is just a reality.

00:02:25.160 --> 00:02:30.050
A lot of these jobs aren't truly jobs that
are over.

00:02:30.050 --> 00:02:31.050
These are furloughs.

00:02:31.050 --> 00:02:34.140
These are sort of like leaves of absence.

00:02:34.140 --> 00:02:37.500
And when these businesses can get going again
and not all of them.

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:42.580
Well, a lot of these jobs are very quickly
going to come off of the unemployment numbers.

00:02:42.580 --> 00:02:44.910
How soon that could be?

00:02:44.910 --> 00:02:45.910
We don't know.

00:02:45.910 --> 00:02:49.620
And of course, the longer this goes, some
businesses aren't going to be able to make

00:02:49.620 --> 00:02:50.870
it through.

00:02:50.870 --> 00:02:51.980
Restaurants are a tragic example.

00:02:51.980 --> 00:02:57.780
Imagine a restaurant in a city with a $5000
a month rent payment, which is not not unusual

00:02:57.780 --> 00:02:58.820
for restaurants in a city.

00:02:58.820 --> 00:03:03.680
Imagine they have, you know, 15 employees
on a regular base basis, including a lot of

00:03:03.680 --> 00:03:04.680
waitstaff.

00:03:04.680 --> 00:03:08.440
Right now, for example, in Massachusetts,
they're doing takeout only.

00:03:08.440 --> 00:03:13.060
There may be down from 15 employees to three
employees, just people cooking, and the owner

00:03:13.060 --> 00:03:17.540
is handling orders because their state has
a stay at home order.

00:03:17.540 --> 00:03:22.070
Their revenue is drastically reduced after
they pay their three employees and they pay

00:03:22.070 --> 00:03:23.820
their rent and utilities.

00:03:23.820 --> 00:03:27.960
They may still be losing money if they don't
get rent support.

00:03:27.960 --> 00:03:33.410
If there aren't rent deferrals at a certain
point, maybe they can do it for a month.

00:03:33.410 --> 00:03:35.480
Maybe they can do it for two months because
they want to keep their business.

00:03:35.480 --> 00:03:38.960
They'll go out of their pocket to keep it
running on a takeout only basis.

00:03:38.960 --> 00:03:42.790
But eventually you're going to see these business
owners start to just walk away.

00:03:42.790 --> 00:03:46.900
And that's why we've got to grin and bear
it now together at the same time.

00:03:46.900 --> 00:03:53.060
If 20 states do stuff now and then 5 stop
and 6 more start next with it, it's not going

00:03:53.060 --> 00:03:54.060
to work.

00:03:54.060 --> 00:03:55.060
Okay.

00:03:55.060 --> 00:03:58.640
If half the country does nothing, we're just
going to extend this and it's going to be

00:03:58.640 --> 00:03:59.760
longer and longer.

00:03:59.760 --> 00:04:04.530
It might be less bad in individual spots for
a little while until it's not.

00:04:04.530 --> 00:04:07.319
We're starting to see Louisiana become a hotspot.

00:04:07.319 --> 00:04:10.260
We're starting to see places now ramp up the
cases.

00:04:10.260 --> 00:04:16.500
The real path is and what Trump should say,
if if Trump again, if Trump is determined

00:04:16.500 --> 00:04:21.600
to say he wants to reopen on Easter, which
is crazy, Trump should say, I want to reopen

00:04:21.600 --> 00:04:24.680
